MID_ADVICE_WeaponRank_001: Bronze
MID_ADVICE_WeaponRank_002: Iron
MID_ADVICE_WeaponRank_003: Da Mina
MID_ADVICE_WeaponRank_004: Silver
MID_ADVICE_JobType_000: Black-Magic Users
MID_ADVICE_JobType_001: White-Magic Users
MID_ADVICE_JobType_002: Cavalry
MID_ADVICE_JobType_003: Heavy Armor
MID_ADVICE_JobType_004: Flying
MID_ADVICE_JobType_005: Ornius Riders
MID_ADVICE_JobType_006: Bow Wielders
MID_ADVICE_JobType_008: Spear Wielders
MID_ADVICE_SC11_04: You seem to be up against a mob of mostly melee types.\nPepper them from afar with bows, magic, and so forth,\nand your victory will be certain.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_05: A slightly more varied crowd, I see. Still, bring the usual\nbows and magic to have a less difficult time. You'll find\nthat equipping bronze weapons will be especially helpful.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_06: I foresee many {LowercaseNextLetter}Charioteers and {Lowercase}Armored Knights{NormalCase}. The\n{LowercaseNextLetter}Charioteers attack with bows, so get in close, and bring\ncasters to negate the high defense of the {Lowercase}Armored Knights{NormalCase}.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_07: Visibility will be poor for your next fight. Tread carefully,\nelse your foes will catch you unaware. Higher-quality\nweapons and magic ought to even the odds.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_09: There appears to be a fondness among your enemies for bows\nto pick you off from afar. I might recommend bringing healing\nitems and magic to compensate.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_10: You're soon to face a powerful foe. Take {Lowercase}Certification Exam{NormalCase}s\nto reach your {LowercaseNextLetter}Specialty classes. Consider allies with strong\ndefense and those skilled in magic attacks.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_11: There's low visibility in your future. 'Twould be wise to bring\nbows and such to counter the enemy's fliers. Is there not some\ndeity's blessing that can clear your sight?
MID_ADVICE_SC11_12: You're likely to face {Lowercase}Ornius Rider{NormalCase}s and {Lowercase}Armored Knights{NormalCase},\nso gird yourself accordingly. White magic and vulneraries\nmay help to soften the blows you'll no doubt receive.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_13: The forces arrayed against you are many, but all will have\ntheir weak points—magic for armored foes, melee for archers,\nand so forth. Any reinforcements will be welcome additions.
MID_ADVICE_SC11_14: This battle will separate you from your allies. A means of\nhealing at a distance would be useful. If the terrain poses\na problem for your mounted units, they can always dismount.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_08: Giant {Lowercase}War Elephant{NormalCase}s will bar your path, but remember that\nspears are an effective counter to any mounted units. Having\nranged weapons and more mobile classes won't go amiss.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_09: Wing soldiers will appear in the next battle—bows should put\npaid to them. Use your {Lowercase}Heavy Armor{NormalCase} units to keep them at\nbay for your bowmen. Watch and wait for your time to strike!
MID_ADVICE_SC12_10: There will be a mob of cavalry enemies with high mobility.\nYou already know what works against them, I trust. Be sure\nnot to get caught in this battle without the right weapons.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_12: Having cavalry capable of covering ground among your allies\nwould be reassuring. Bringing bows in the event of any enemy\nfliers may improve your chances as well.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_14: The terrain ahead, I'm afraid, is murky with poor footing.\nFor good measure, have as many allies as you can advance\nto their {LowercaseNextLetter}Specialty classes through {Lowercase}Certification Exams{NormalCase}.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_15: A class capable of bypassing low obstacles could be handy for\nbreaching the enemy lines. Your foes' assault will rain down\nfuriously, so bring hardy and resistant units to withstand it.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_16: Beware of traps underfoot! You will face a mix of flying and\ninfantry squads, so you must plan to deal with both types of\ntroops if you hope to prevail.
MID_ADVICE_SC12_17: To engage your foes, you must split your forces. Any support\nthey can lend from a distance will be invaluable. Have you\nanyone who excels with ranged attacks like bows or magic?
MID_ADVICE_SC13_04: Your opponent is rather skilled, hm? Beware those quick\nmovements and deadly strikes! Allies who can take a beating\nwill help, as well as healers to keep them on their feet.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_07: Though the enemy appears to be few in number, I would be\nwary all the same. I have an ominous feeling about this...\nYou'd do well to prepare yourself for undead foes.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_09: Take heed of the poison your foes employ! You'd do well to\nhave an antidote to it on hand. This may be the time to take\n{Lowercase}Certification Exam{NormalCase}s for your {LowercaseNextLetter}Specialty classes.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_10: Ugh, these horrible beasts are far too large! A hunter's\nbow would be a useful countermeasure. Their bite is\nvenomous, so be prepared with an antidote.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_11: 'Twould seem you and your foe are vying for some prize.\nThe clan who collects the most is the winner, so keep a\nspot open in your inventory for the special baubles.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_12: You'll face many foes who attack from a distance, using bows\nand magic both. Best to bring allies highly resistant to such\ntactics in order to bear the brunt.
MID_ADVICE_SC13_13: Assaulting an impregnable fortress, are we? You'll face all\nmanner of foe, including those capable of taking out your\nvaunted cavalry. Keep your allies well-protected!
MID_ADVICE_SC14_05: Normal weapons will do little against the heavily armored\nsoldiers you'll face. Magic may fare better. If your current\nforces seem thin, recruit more allies.
MID_ADVICE_SC14_06: You'll be facing hardy soldiers with thick defenses, but they\nwon't be prepared for your black magic. An axe or two may\nalso help to split their heavy armor.
MID_ADVICE_SC14_09: This will be your first battle against the risen dead of the\nunderworld. Have you any weapons capable of opposing\nthem? Don't forget to make good use of the onagers!
MID_ADVICE_SC14_12: Take {Lowercase}Certification Exams{NormalCase} to graduate to {LowercaseNextLetter}Specialty classes.\nIdeally, you'll count among your units those with high defense,\nan aptitude for magic, and the ability to attack at range.
MID_ADVICE_SC14_13: Walls will divide your forces, but you may rise to the\nchallenge with allies who can withstand punishment—or,\nfailing that, anyone who can heal from a distance.
MID_ADVICE_SC14_14: Ugh, 'tis the risen dead again. Don't stint on weaponry\ncapable of damaging them! I'd also advise cavalry with high\nmobility to take the fight to them.
MID_ADVICE_SC14_15: Your foes will bring all their considerable power down on you\nin the next battle, striking at range with bows and spells.\nBring allies who can withstand and recover from their assault.
MID_ADVICE_SC30_00: A great war begins... Are you all of {LowercaseNextLetter}Advanced classes yet?\nIf not, hurry and take your exams. And bring a variety of\nallies who can handle whatever foes may come. Best of luck!
MID_ADVICE_SC30_01: Are any of you still not {LowercaseNextLetter}Advanced? Best address that if so.\nBeyond that, you'll want soldiers who can cover great\ndistances—whatever cavalry and flying units you possess.
MID_ADVICE_SC30_03: This battlefield will constrain your advance with narrow\npassages. Turn them to your advantage by having armored\nunits hold choke points while archers pepper your foes!
MID_ADVICE_SC30_05: You may be beset by a rush of flying foes. Face them\nfearlessly with bows in hand! So long as you don't neglect\nsome means of recovery, you can withstand a few injuries.
MID_ADVICE_SC30_06: A dreadfully powerful foe awaits you. Do not approach\nrecklessly—send your best-trained allies and attack from\nbeyond his range with your finest bows and spells.
MID_ADVICE_SC30_07: You will doubtless face the armies of the underworld. Bring\nweapons they are vulnerable to and press onward! Don't\nneglect any aspect of your forces—classes, weapons, or items!
MID_ADVICE_SC00_07: Dangerous miasma spews from the gate, surrounding it.\nIt is the sort that will drain your vitality—train your allies well\nthat they might withstand it.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_13: Has anyone reached the level of {LowercaseNextLetter}Master yet? If not, strive for\nthat. The miasma you'll face here will crumble your weapons\naway, so stay clear of it. Or perhaps use a deity's blessing?
MID_ADVICE_SC00_11: Our foes are growing tougher. Are you ensuring your allies\nreach {LowercaseNextLetter}Master classes? The miasma on this battlefield affects\none's aim...but perhaps we can turn that to our advantage.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_08: Our battles grow more intense. I hope you are collecting\n{LowercaseNextLetter}Master licenses! Visibility is poor on this battlefield, especially\nin the miasma. A blessing of far sight would be most welcome.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_12: This gate's miasma can confuse your accuracy and ability to\ndodge. Be quite prepared before you sally forth. Master classes\nare a must, and divine classes may be desirable at this point.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_09: This gate's miasma can confuse your accuracy and ability to\ndodge—but it can be negated if you're sharp. Master classes\nare a must, plus as many divine classes as you can muster.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_10: This gate's miasma both grants and siphons strength, for you\nas well as your enemy. Master classes are a must, and the\nmore divine classes you can muster, the better.
MID_ADVICE_SC00_14: The critical moment is here at last. This fight will be long and\ngrueling. Bring the highest-caliber weapons and gear, and\nthink carefully on your abilities and assignments.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_00: You must not allow the enemy to reach their objective.\nAllies with high mobility will be useful both to obstruct your\nfoe's path and to access helpful features of the battlefield.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_01: An onslaught of foes will attempt to thwart you. Block them\nwith your hardiest units, and keep healers on hand so they\ndon't fall. Everyone must work together on defense.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_02: Your vision will be obscured here. Take allies with staunch\ndefense to ward against surprise attacks. Or better yet, invoke\na blessing to see your foes approach.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_03: These beasts you face are nimble, and venomous as well.\nTake measures to deal with both the beasts and the poison.\nArmored warriors can help you ward off their advances.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_04: This battle will pit you against several large foes. I might\nsuggest allies with high defense or greater mobility. Magic\nand long-range weapons may also be useful.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_05: Any counters you have for large, flying foes will be invaluable\nfor this battle. Classes with superior mobility will be wanted\nfor chasing down any troublesome foes.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_06: The terrain is complex and your foes are legion. Be ready to\ndeal with any and all circumstances. If pressed, I'd say you'd\ndo well to have someone skilled with black magic.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_07: Large, venomous beasts will block your escape. Keep the way\nclear with weapons suited for beasts and antidotes to their\ntoxins. The ability to cover more ground will also be useful.
MID_ADVICE_SCXX_08: A large foe will prove troublesome here. Magic and bow users\ncan't go amiss when dealing with changing circumstances.\nA variety of allies will help you to adapt to the flow of battle.
